92186115458 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186048420 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115458 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "cf42fdc1-dee5-53a6-abe0-79ec4ef7b900" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186116351 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186116354 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186116351 #edb/ref 1061 615 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186116351 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "62b549c4-9fa6-595c-9705-edecd57fab60" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186116351 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186116507 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186116352 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186116355 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186116352 #edb/ref 1061 616 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186116352 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "7d001457-3a19-5fb6-b582-e4447e917a71" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186116352 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186115380 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186116353 #edb/ref 1061 619 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186116353 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "d3a114b6-40b8-5189-a0c2-30250448ba57" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186116353 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186115381 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186116354 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186116352 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186116354 #edb/ref 1061 622 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186116354 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "872a7f94-c8a5-5f55-a91f-39909aca384f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186116354 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186116514 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186116355 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186116353 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186116355 #edb/ref 1061 623 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186116355 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "4284ae9c-1207-5fcc-829e-569528302322" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186116355 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186115382 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186116507 #edb/ref 1064 "A function $f(x)$ is said to be **differentiable** at a point $x=a$ if the derivative $f'(a)$ exists.\n\nIn general:\n\n- If a function is not continuous at some point, then it is not differentiable at that point either.\n\n- If a function is differentiable at some point, then it must be continuous at that point.\n\nFor example, suppose we are given a step function $y=f(x)$ that has a jump discontinuity at $x=3,$ given below. We will verify that $f(x)$ is not differentiable at $x=3$ by showing that $f'(3)$ does not exist. \n\n![](images/9f/9f91b034a27ce7fd2b432f0b094e4b40098247916b78f9c1b3eb64c7214f69b4.png)\n\nThe value $f'(3)$ is a limit, so to check whether it exists, we need to compute the left and right-sided limits.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{'}(3)={lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{f(x)-f(3)}{x-3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs $x$ approaches $3$ from the left, we have that $f(x) = 2.$ So the left-sided limit is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {3}^{-}}\\frac{f(x)-f(3)}{x-3} & ={lim}_{x\\to {3}^{-}}\\frac{2-2}{x-3}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, as $x$ approaches $3$ from the right, we have that $f(x)=1.$ So the right-sided limit is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {3}^{+}}\\frac{f(x)-f(3)}{x-3} & ={lim}_{x\\to {3}^{+}}\\frac{1-2}{x-3}={lim}_{x\\to {3}^{+}}\\frac{-1}{x-3}=-\\infty .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBecause the left and right-sided limits are not equal, the overall limit does not exist. \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{'}(3)={lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{f(x)-f(3)}{x-3}=\\text{DNE}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $f(x)$ is not differentiable at $x=3.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186116507 #edb/ref 1065 332 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186116507 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "60845968-f9d5-58f2-9205-7c60bc949ed6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186116507 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186116514 #edb/ref 1064 "If a function is continuous, that does *not* mean that it's differentiable!\n\nTo demonstrate, let's consider the function $f(x)=|x|.$ The function $f(x)$ is continuous everywhere, including the point $x=0.$ But is $f(x)$ also differentiable everywhere? \n\n![](images/18/18644551713e0c1d451cf27bd43f3cc8fc8d7064d7af79df3cd2070af782c25e.png)\n\nFor $x < 0,$ the graph consists of a downwards-sloping line with slope $-1.$ For $x > 0,$ the graph consists of an upward-sloping line with slope $1.$ So, the derivative of the absolute value function is given by\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-1\\, & x<0, \\\\ 1\\, & x>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the derivative of $f(x)=|x|$ does not exist at $x=0.$ This is because the limit of the slope as we approach $x=0$ from the left is not equal to the limit as we approach from the right.\n\nIn general, a continuous function $f(x)$ is not differentiable at $x=a$ if the function $f(x)$ has any of the following features:\n\n- A **corner point** at $x=a.$ For example, $f(x)=|x|$ at $x=0.$\n\n- A **cusp** at $x=a.$ For example, $f(x) = \\sqrt{|x|}$ at $x=0.$\n\n- A **vertical tangent** at $x=a.$ For example, $f(x)=\\sqrt[3]{x}$ at $x=0.$\n\n![](images/28/28a6f3a424556e1e60e4959b03a5c38a1ff6a5d0efb110a0e5a4bfadc7072511.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186116514 #edb/ref 1065 335 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186116514 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "0df8723a-c6d6-562d-8cde-b44a47dd70bc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186116514 #edb/ref 1067 "Continuity Does Not Imply Differentiability" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186236382 #edb/ref 1080 "II only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186236382 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186236382 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "5a423260-bbbe-5ae5-9f27-db48fce5a7d4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186236384 #edb/ref 1080 "II and III only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186236384 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186236384 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "5b27cad1-42d8-5307-8cc2-5cc48adae5ed" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186236804 #edb/ref 1080 "III only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186236804 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186236804 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "9dce0a55-5641-528c-9f93-21ec3cd96888" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237400 #edb/ref 1080 "I and II only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237400 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237400 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "fa19be47-2169-5673-84c3-412cf1b7a226" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237439 #edb/ref 1080 "I and III only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237439 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237439 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "feda186f-19bf-5fb8-9907-6309e3735091" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237738 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186236382 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237738 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186236384 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237738 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186236804 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237738 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186237400 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237738 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186237439 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237738 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237738 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237738 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186236384 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237738 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "e8ff4376-b626-5cd5-b078-07242fef4809" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237867 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186237738 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237867 #edb/ref 1069 "q-101995" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237867 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237867 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that a function $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=0$, has a removable discontinuity at $x=1$, and is differentiable at $x=-1$, which of the following statements must be true for **any** $f(x)$ that satisfy these criteria?\n\n- It is differentiable at $x=0$\n- It  is **not** differentiable at $x=1$\n- It is continuous at $x=-1$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237867 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0efb43bb-72c2-5796-b21b-537b0708d8ce" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237867 #edb/ref 1074 "- Statement I is false. Continuity does not imply differentiability. For example, the function $y=|x|$ is continuous but it's not differentiable at $x=0.$\n\n- Statement II is true.  A function that is discontinuous at a point can't be differentiable at this point (because differentiability implies continuity).\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, differentiability implies continuity." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186327214 #edb/ref 1080 "II and III only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186327214 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186327214 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "20ac00fa-c573-50b2-9181-c5c47c436adb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186327822 #edb/ref 1080 "II only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186327822 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186327822 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "6664d395-2cd4-57fa-8267-dad7b7f6653c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186328441 #edb/ref 1080 "I and III only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186328441 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186328441 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "ad7699cf-1310-5e2c-8483-50775b4a0f7d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186328700 #edb/ref 1080 "I and II only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186328700 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186328700 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "c8d74407-8722-5f57-a238-174a8da68bde" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186328760 #edb/ref 1080 "III only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186328760 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186328760 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "cf91c4ec-315b-5bb2-ba9b-e695b2ead9ad" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329187 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186327214 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329187 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186327822 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329187 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186328441 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329187 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186328700 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329187 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186328760 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329187 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329187 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329187 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186327822 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329187 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "01e41401-65d6-5b8b-a09b-c7db46fa5956" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329826 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186329187 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329826 #edb/ref 1069 "q-47681" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329826 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329826 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function given below?\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3}+1, & x\\ne 1 \\\\ 3, & x=1\\end{aligned}\\,\n$$\n\n- It is continuous and differentiable at $x=1$\n- It is **not** differentiable at $x=1$\n- It is differentiable on the interval $(-1,2)$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329826 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8298d153-fa1d-58c6-bfcd-efab6041f9f0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329826 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's analyze each statement individually. \n\n- Statement I is false.  At $x=1$, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {1}^{+}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {1}^{+}}({x}^{3}+1)={1}^{3}+1=2 \\\\ {lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}({x}^{3}+1)={1}^{3}+1=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {1}^{+}}f(x)={lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}f(x)\\ne f(1)=3,\n$$\n\nand so $f(x)$ is not continuous at $x=1$ ($f(x)$ has a removable discontinuity at $x=1$).\n\n- Statement II is true. Since  $f(x)$ is not continuous at $x=1,$ it is also not differentiable there (because differentiability implies continuity).\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $f(x)$ is not differentiable at $x=1,$ it is not differentiable on any interval containing this point. Consequently, it is not differentiable on $(-1,2).$\n\nTherefore, only statement II is true." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339559 #edb/ref 1080 "I and II only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339559 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339559 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3115a701-908d-5194-89b5-3934f2aee943" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339696 #edb/ref 1080 "III only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339696 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339696 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3ef63771-16e0-5c66-87bb-9773a47f39ce" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339705 #edb/ref 1080 "I and III only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339705 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339705 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "4084d34d-cdd6-5521-90d7-5d09fec010be" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339717 #edb/ref 1080 "III only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339717 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339717 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "43206143-d3e7-5558-906d-23db6302ae10" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339951 #edb/ref 1080 "II only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339951 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339951 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "5aac758e-2f12-517d-8ce4-fe8a5696f212" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339975 #edb/ref 1080 "I only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339975 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339975 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "5f7cee9c-67f1-509a-a047-56e0f6f1ef9b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186340536 #edb/ref 1080 "I and II only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186340536 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186340536 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "9c49a7a3-a3b7-5ac2-9f14-8aeb96443d71" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186340567 #edb/ref 1080 "II only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186340567 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186340567 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "9f5901ab-7568-583f-a1e8-bd3745447399" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186340822 #edb/ref 1080 "I only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186340822 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186340822 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "be0a87e6-ce52-5475-84fa-d3314aa5b89d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341093 #edb/ref 1080 "I and III only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341093 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341093 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "dd1f61f7-02e8-5317-a136-be60633289a9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341466 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186339717 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341466 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186339951 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341466 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186340536 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341466 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186340822 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341466 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186341093 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341466 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341466 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341466 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186341093 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341466 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "315e5c79-1bab-5a2f-a733-2981ea179e3a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341640 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186339559 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341640 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186339696 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341640 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186339705 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341640 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186339975 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341640 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186340567 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341640 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341640 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341640 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186340567 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341640 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "941f6918-d68b-5b25-9b9f-c8698c202566" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341928 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186341640 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341928 #edb/ref 1069 "q-73250" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341928 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341928 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/a8/a8a70a2f28585b63d2a083b42eb6ad54bfb581b5f13c699a3bc3c8d836afaee8.png)\n\nGiven the plot of the function $y=f(x)$ above, which of the following statements are true?\n\n- The function is continuous at $x=1$\n- The function is continuous at $x=0$\n- The function is differentiable at $x=0$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341928 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "fa88d46b-d2ce-5164-bbed-10d691e29ef6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341928 #edb/ref 1074 "- Statement I is false. From the graph we can see that $f(x)$ has a removable discontinuity at $x=1.$\n\n- Statement II is true. The graph can be drawn in a neighborhood of $x=0$ without taking the pencil off the paper.\n\n- Statement III is false. The function $f(x)$ has a corner point at $x=0$ and so it is not differentiable there.\n\nTherefore, only statement II is true." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341929 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186341466 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341929 #edb/ref 1069 "q-73252" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341929 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341929 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/1f/1f2d8b9faac6c300b41902cea5065bf8bafb02c137232ee79779a4dc3ff67f33.png)\n\nGiven the plot of the function $y=f(x)$ above, which of the following statements are true?\n\n- The function is continuous at $x=-1$\n- The function is differentiable at $x=1$\n- The function is continuous at $x=2$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341929 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "fb7ec702-6570-50d7-8199-a59c190c3e40" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341929 #edb/ref 1074 "- Statement I is true. The graph can be drawn in a neighborhood of $x=-1$ without taking the pencil off the paper.\n\n- Statement II is false. From the graph we can see that $f(x)$ has a removable discontinuity at $x=1.$ So, it can't be differentiable there.\n\n- Statement III is true. The graph can be drawn in a neighborhood of $x=2$ without taking the pencil off the paper.\n\nTherefore, only statements I and III  are true." #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
